{"content":[{"c":["BETH-SHEMESH"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. Canaanite city on the northern border of Judah’s territory (",{"href":"?bref=Josh.15.10","r":"Josh.15.10","rawR":"Josh.15.10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.15.10","value":"Josh.15.10"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jos 15:10"},") and the southern border of Dan’s (before that tribe migrated north). Beth-shemesh means “the house of Shamash,” the Canaanite sun god. As Ir-shemesh, it was included in the list of cities of Dan (",{"href":"?bref=Josh.19.41","r":"Josh.19.41","rawR":"Josh.19.41","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.19.41","value":"Josh.19.41"}],"t":"ref","v":"19:41"},"). Beth-shemesh was one of the towns of Judah granted to the Levites (",{"href":"?bref=Josh.21.16","r":"Josh.21.16","rawR":"Josh.21.16","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.21.16","value":"Josh.21.16"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jos 21:16"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.6.59","r":"1Chr.6.59","rawR":"1Chr.6.59","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.6.59","value":"1Chr.6.59"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 6:59"},"). Its inhabitants were called Beth-shemites (",{"href":"?bref=1Sam.6.14,18","r":"1Sam.6.14,18","rawR":"1Sam.6.14,18","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Sam.6.14,18","value":"1Sam.6.14,18"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Sm 6:14, 18"},", ",{"c":["kjv"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"},"). When the Philistines decided to dispose of the captured ark of the covenant because plagues were breaking out in their cities, they took it to Beth-shemesh. The area was also the scene of a great victory of King Joash (Jehoash) of Israel over King Amaziah of Judah (",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.25.21-23","r":"2Chr.25.21-23","rawR":"2Chr.25.21-23","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.25.21-23","value":"2Chr.25.21-23"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chr 25:21-23"},"). About a century later, Beth-shemesh was captured from King Ahaz of Judah by the Philistines (",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.28.16-20","r":"2Chr.28.16-20","rawR":"2Chr.28.16-20","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.28.16-20","value":"2Chr.28.16-20"}],"t":"ref","v":"28:16-20"},"). After that, the settlement fell into decline and was finally destroyed by Nebuchadnezzar in 586 ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"},"."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["2. Canaanite city allotted to Issachar’s tribe (",{"href":"?bref=Josh.19.22","r":"Josh.19.22","rawR":"Josh.19.22","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.19.22","value":"Josh.19.22"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jos 19:22"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["3. Fortified Canaanite city allotted to Naphtali’s tribe (",{"href":"?bref=Josh.19.38","r":"Josh.19.38","rawR":"Josh.19.38","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.19.38","value":"Josh.19.38"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jos 19:38"},"). The inhabitants of this Beth-shemesh were not driven out by the Israelites (",{"href":"?bref=Judg.1.33","r":"Judg.1.33","rawR":"Judg.1.33","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Judg.1.33","value":"Judg.1.33"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jgs 1:33"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["4. KJV reference to the Egyptian city of Heliopolis (or On), where the sun was worshiped (",{"href":"?bref=Jer.43.13","r":"Jer.43.13","rawR":"Jer.43.13","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.43.13","value":"Jer.43.13"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jer 43:13"},"). ",{"c":["See"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=Heliopolis_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"Heliopolis_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"Heliopolis_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Heliopolis"},"."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"BethShemesh","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Jos 15:10","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.15.10","rawQueryValue":"Josh.15.10","sourceRefExact":"Josh.15.10"},{"anchorText":"19:41","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.19.41","rawQueryValue":"Josh.19.41","sourceRefExact":"Josh.19.41"},{"anchorText":"Jos 21:16","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.21.16","rawQueryValue":"Josh.21.16","sourceRefExact":"Josh.21.16"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 6:59","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.6.59","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.6.59","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.6.59"},{"anchorText":"1 Sm 6:14, 18","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Sam.6.14,18","rawQueryValue":"1Sam.6.14,18","sourceRefExact":"1Sam.6.14,18"},{"anchorText":"2 Chr 25:21-23","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Chr.25.21-23","rawQueryValue":"2Chr.25.21-23","sourceRefExact":"2Chr.25.21-23"},{"anchorText":"28:16-20","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Chr.28.16-20","rawQueryValue":"2Chr.28.16-20","sourceRefExact":"2Chr.28.16-20"},{"anchorText":"Jos 19:22","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.19.22","rawQueryValue":"Josh.19.22","sourceRefExact":"Josh.19.22"},{"anchorText":"Jos 19:38","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.19.38","rawQueryValue":"Josh.19.38","sourceRefExact":"Josh.19.38"},{"anchorText":"Jgs 1:33","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Judg.1.33","rawQueryValue":"Judg.1.33","sourceRefExact":"Judg.1.33"},{"anchorText":"Jer 43:13","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Jer.43.13","rawQueryValue":"Jer.43.13","sourceRefExact":"Jer.43.13"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"b7872645e6f56093bc9780c59c624f7259b3e751b0e9d396eec74da9a224fe05","sourceItemName":"BethShemesh","sourceItemOrder":277,"sourceMember":"Articles/B.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[{"name":"AerialViewOfBethShemesh","src":"../Pictures/Pictures.xml"}]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"BethShemesh","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Beth-Shemesh","title":"Beth-Shemesh","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}